A||N||17||Archie||Need Help with Lap Top||||5||
Z||000000||Archie||12-21-2001||08:26 PM||||Ok, a year or so ago, I bought a new laptop at Best Buy. It is a Toshiba "Satellite" 1605CDS/4.3<P>I have 2 little problems with it that keep me from using it very much.<P>1st problem is that on a full charge it will only run for about 20 minutes before it shuts down for lack of power. I was thinking that maybe I didn't "deep cycle" the battery enough initially thus shortening the battery cycle life. I've already went and bought another new battery and was careful to charge it properly as instructed. That didn't really help, the life of a full charge is still only like 20 munutes.<P>Anyway the other problem (if I find an answer to this problem it would negate the need to solve problem one. 2nd problem.... I want to be able to re-charge and power the lap top from the car cigg. lighter. Does anyone know Where and what kind of Cigg. lighter re-charger/adapter I need to get?<P>Thanks<P>Archie||||reg||5
Z||000001||Loki||12-21-2001||08:34 PM||||I know alot of laptops will drain the battery fast..I had an older Toshiba that would drain in in about that time..Maybe just the way ti is, though you might look at "longer lasting" batteries. I know they make em. And as far as cig lighter goes, I havnt a clue. Good luck with it Archie..<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fieroloki.com/lokisig1%20copy.jpg">   <BR>"All Fieros broke right now" :(||||reg||1
Z||000002||ejayerik||12-21-2001||08:38 PM||||It can be fixed but it will cost a good buck. The high charge batterys are not cheap. Though it may be the laptop. See if the batterys are memory free batterys. BTW..I'll give you 300 bucks for your laptop if you want to get rid of it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Adrift||12-21-2001||09:00 PM||||A) Short battery - if your battery is under warranty, just call up toshiba and tell them it lasts for under 10 minutes... they will replace it for you. Rule of thumb: Laptop batterys suck. Pick up a new one off ebay, will cost you 1/5th of what Toshiba will charge.<P>b) To plug in the car the best way to go is  get a voltage coverter/adapter which coverts DC to AC, costs about $45 here in Canada, and does the job quite nicely.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Devotshka||12-22-2001||12:29 AM||||Regardless of the mAh rating 20 minutes is definately way too short.  Check and see if the battery is showing 100% in the bios.  Since the problem carried over to the new battery, i'd check the contacts inside the laptop for the battery.  Sounds like you have some corrosion in there or a poor connection.||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroSTETZ||12-22-2001||03:24 AM||||I personally am a TAT toshiba associate technician- most likely, the power management in your system is all wacked out- on order to pull off the legendary "2 hour batter life" you need to enable speedstep (if so equipped) remove any removable drives, have as little memory installed as possible, run in 16 bit color, without sound, and turn down your brightness. i am looking through the toshiba service atlas right now to see if i have any better recommendations. if you decide to replace the laptop, think about a used apple powerbook g3, or a new g4- my g3 lasts about 4 hours on a battery, and has room for 2 of them- the g4 has 1 battery, and lasts about 5 hours. keep in mind, if your computer is on, constantly being used, or has a screensaver rahter than a screen shitoff, then you will be wasting juice. the best battery life i have seen yet was out of a tosghiba s401, we turned the harddrive to park after 1 minute, display 1 minute, system suspend 5 minutes, processor speed minimum- and got 3 hours- but the machine was nearly unusable.<P><BR>as far as mobile charging- get a power inverter from radio shack- not only provides a wall outlet, but acts as a surge protector as well. if you go straight from a cig lighter to the laptop, then your electrical output will vary w/ the rpm of the car. this is BAD- use an inverter. if you need any more info, or have other questions, email me at fierostetz@home.com- ttyl!||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroSTETZ||12-22-2001||03:27 AM||||POWER  <BR>Autosensing External AC Adapter Part Number: PA3032U-1ACA <BR>Dimensions/Weight 4.2" W x 2.4" H x 1.2" D, --- Weight: .6lbs. <BR>Input (Voltage/Frequency) 90-264V; 47-63Hz <BR>Output (Voltage/Amps) 19VDC; 2.4A  <BR>Power Output (Watts) 45W <BR>Battery Type: NiMH (10.8V, 3800mAH) Yes one standard: Part# PA3031U-1BRS <BR>Dimensions/Weight<BR> 5.5"L x 4.25"W x .95"H --- Weight: 1.2 lbs. <BR>Battery Life: (Full Power)  2.2 hrs <BR>Recharge Time (Computer Off/On)  2/3 hrs. depending on the computer function performed <BR>Power Saving Features ACPI (1.0b), Stand By, Hibernation <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||watts||12-22-2001||03:46 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroSTETZ:<BR><B>I personally am a TAT toshiba associate technician- </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not meaning to hijack Archie's thread, but...  I have a Toshiba 435CDS.  It's only got the CD, no floppy!  I want to get ahold of the original install CD so I have all the drivers, etc.  Any chance you could find this and send my an ISO or whatever?  This will boot off the CD, right?  If not, I'm screwed with no floppy!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||thomas_l||12-22-2001||07:45 AM||||I can't speak specifically for Toshiba, but you got a bad battery. Even with power management turned off and accessories installed you should get at least one hour out of a full charge.<P>Another thing - until about a year ago most laptops shipped with NiMh batteries. They do get a memory and I don't care what the experts say, they are good for about a year then they turn into paperweights. Toshiba's online store has them for $39. Of course if it's under warranty Best Buy ought to exchange yours no charge but they may put you through the hassle of testing it to prove the bad battery.<P>Newer systems have Lithium-Ion batteries that charge faster and have nearly no memory effect. I use a Compaq Armada and get 2.5 - 3 hours on the main battery and another 1.5 hours if I remove the CD and use the aux battery. On a long flight watching DVD movies (with the DVD drive constantly running) will burn up the main battery in around 2 hours so I pack a spare  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||rogergarrison||12-22-2001||11:55 AM||||Ive got a Toshiba 1555CDS, almost same as yours. Its two years old. I use dimmer mode to save power, and dont use the screensaver on bat power. I still get between 1 1/2 and 2 hours on a full charge. I see aftermarket cig liter adapters in catalogs like Heartland, Techno Stuff all the time for around 60-70 dollars. If your interested I can go thru a bunch of them and find one. It is handy being able to use my laptop with my cellphone to get on net like at car shows, Hooters, etc, or even pulled over in a rest area.||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroSTETZ||12-22-2001||02:38 PM||||unfortunately, as almost all manufacturers, toshiba refuses to warranty the battery after 14 days- no matter what- its considered a consumable, as with hinges- good luck w/ best buy, but they wont get reimbursement from toshiba, and its not likeley that they will BUY him a battery.||||reg||1
Z||000011||SteveJ||12-22-2001||05:08 PM||||Targus air/auto power transformer Model #PA375U <A HREF="http://www.targus.com/accessories_power.asp?pos=2" TARGET=_blank>http://www.targus.com/accessories_power.asp?pos=2</A> <P>Bought mine at <A HREF="http://www.provantage.com/for" TARGET=_blank>www.provantage.com/for</A>  $88.61   <BR>Brand name item / reliable supplier.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Archie||12-22-2001||06:33 PM||||You guys have been a lot more help than you know.<P>I'm not going to buy another battery because I just bought a new one & it didn't clear up the problem. I will try a few power saving things on my unit but the thing I really want to do is plug the laptop into the cigg lighter so that I can use the laptop in the car. <P>If I can get the batt. on the laptop to last me 30 to 45 minutes on a charge then being able to recharge it in the car will serve my needs just fine.<P>It looks like I can hook that thing up to the car for less than $100, so that's what I'll look into doing.<P>Thanks<P>Archie<P><P>------------------<BR>Just how fast do you want to go?||||reg||1
Z||000013||watts||12-23-2001||01:50 AM||||Hey Arch - although I can't really do it in the Fiero for lack of space, what I did in my last car was to mount the inverter under a seat, hard wired it into the 12V, then made up a 120V outlet box which I mounted sorta under the dash beside the console.  Nice easy access for whatever (laptop adaptor, drop lamp, etc).<P>By the way, that 20 min's is awful - my older machine (old battery, not in power save mode, etc) will still get about an hour or more of life to it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||The Fieromaster||12-23-2001||04:59 AM||||Archie...<P>How do you charge the battery?  Maybe somthing is wrong with the charging system so that it reads the battery as being full when its really only 20% or so!?!?<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">        <FONT COLOR="red"><B>"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT></B>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thefieromastersig.gif">    <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AOL IM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B>||||reg||1
Z||000015||thomas_l||12-23-2001||06:29 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by The Fieromaster:<BR><B>Archie...<P>How do you charge the battery?  Maybe somthing is wrong with the charging system so that it reads the battery as being full when its really only 20% or so!?!?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Good point. On my Armada there is a feature in power management (Win2k) that recalibrates the battery %charge display by doing a measured discharge. Maybe yours has that too...||||reg||1
Z||000016||Formula88||12-23-2001||03:52 PM||||I don't remember the Toshiba warranty off the top of my head, but IBM batteries are warrantied for 1 year.  I'd imagine Toshiba would be at least 90 days.<P>Like FieroSTETZ said, it's most likely in your power settings.  CDROMS, sound, and your LCD eat the majority of your power.  If you disable sound (not just mute or turn the volume down) you'll get much more battery life.  Also, run the LCD as dimm as comfortable and set your power management to enable "speedstepping" of the CPU.  Make sure the Hard Drive idle time is set to something like 1-3 minutes, otherwise it's spinning all the time, even when you're not accessing it.<P>I've got an IBM ThinkPad A21e and even with the power management set to High Performance (full speed, bright LCD, all options running), I still get almost 2 hours out of my battery.  You may want to have your laptop checked.  It may not be properly charging the battery.  <P>Are you using a Li-Ion battery?  They are "memory proof", well, memory resistant.... And they last longer.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Archie||12-23-2001||06:44 PM||||So far so good........ I've tried as many of your suggestions as I can figure out how to do, & it appears that my batt life is up to an hour. <P>If I was a youngster I would be embarresed by my lack of knowledge in this area. However, being an old fart, I have an excuse for being a PC idiot.<P>I have yet to figure out how to do that measured discharge and I'm at a loss as to how to disable the sound. I'm working with Win98.<P>Thanks All.<P>I'll try to find the correct thing to hook my pc up to the cigg lighter tomorrow and then this laptop might get some extended use.<P>Archie||||reg||1
